<!--
==================================================================================
  WIX L&D  ·  PRACTICE SESSION  ·  INTERACTIVE SCENARIO TEMPLATE  (Rise Code Block)
  v2 — Wix-branded redesign. SAME interaction/scoring model as v1; look only.

Last Revision Date : 09/10/26 07:12pm

==================================================================================

  HOW TO READ THIS FILE (for stakeholders / non-coders)
  -----------------------------------------------------
  Two parts, on purpose:
    1) THE SCENARIO  (<script id="scenario">) — the CONTENT. Reads like a table.
    2) THE ENGINE    (<script id="engine">)   — the machinery that plays ANY scenario.

  WHAT CHANGED IN v2 (design only — the model below is unchanged)
  --------------------------------------------------------------
    • Wix Madefor typography (Display for headings, Text for body) via Google Fonts.
    • Three phases in one self-contained embed: MEET THE USER → LIVE CHAT → COMPLETE.
    • The live chat mirrors the real Wix Communication Panel: gray customer bubbles
      (left), blue agent bubbles (right), a call timer, and a red "End" button.
      (No sentiment chip — deliberately omitted.)
    • Brand palette applied. The END scorecard keeps the locked correctness legend
      (green / amber / red · done / partial / missed) — unchanged.
    • Helper pop-ups use the native <dialog> element (MDN-recommended for modals).

  THE INTERACTION MODEL (unchanged from v1)
  -----------------------------------------
  Each scenario mirrors a real Expert <-> user interaction across eight graded
  behaviors (the rubric, 100 pts):
     open(5) · dynamics(10) · familiarize(10) · clarify(15)
     roadmap(10) · article(20) · recreate(10) · solve(20)

  Rules:
    • FEEDBACK IS SAVED FOR THE END. No grade, no correctness colors, no running
      score during play. Choosing an answer simply advances the call.
    • IN-CHARACTER REACTIONS ARE NOT FEEDBACK. A weak choice may draw a caller
      reaction in dialogue; that line is part of the sim, not a grade.
    • MOSTLY GATED, SOME FREEDOM — "gate:true" screens must be finished to advance.
    • RETRY ONLY IF THE USER PROMPTS — a choice marked "retry:true" re-opens the
      screen because the caller pushed back; the retry is capped by "capIfRetried".
    • SKIPS ARE RECOVERABLE — each stage keeps its own best score.
    • ROADMAP FLOATS — attach roadmap credit to any choice via credits:[...].

  FIELD GUIDE
  -----------
    user   : { name, image, bio } — shown on the MEET screen and in the call header.
    STAGE  : id, name, max, strength (shown at end if done), improvement (if missed).
    SCREEN : stage, gate, speaker (caller line), prompt, choices[].
    CHOICE : text, verdict, points, goTo, credits[], retry/capIfRetried,
             consequence, stageOverride.
==================================================================================
-->

